laimed control over all 32 Irish counties, including Ulster, and the IAAF demanded that they be in charge of only the 26 counties of the Irish Free State. Thus, O’Callaghan was not allowed to compete. He would have been favored again, throwing 59.56 (195-5) in 1937, well above the world record (although it was not recognized)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In O’Callaghan’s absence, the first two places were taken by Germans, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/70271"} "Karl Hein"] " winning a big upset victory. He trailed his countryman " [:a {:href "/athletes/70161"} "Erwin Blask"] " until the final throw, but came thru in the last round with 56.49 (185-4) to secure the gold medal. In 1938, Blask would throw 59.00 (193-7) to break the long-standing world record of 57.77 (189-6½), set by " [:a {:href "/athletes/78986"} "Paddy Ryan"] " in 1913."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "883"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/70271"} "Karl Hein"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "– (" [:span {:class "label label-primary"} [:abbrev {:title "Also Competed"} "AC"]] ")"] [:td {} "56.49 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "881"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/70161"} "Erwin Blask"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "– (" [:span {:class "label label-primary"} [:abbrev {:title "Also Competed"} "AC"]] ")"]